  "question": {
    "text": "A pulley of radius $2 \\mathrm{~m}$ is rotated about its axis by a force $\\mathrm{F}=\\left(20 \\mathrm{t}-5 \\mathrm{t}^2\\right)$ Newton (where $\\mathrm{t}$ is measured in seconds) applied tangentially. If the moment of inertia of the pulley about its axis of rotation made by the pulley before its direction of motion if reversed, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "UjhvZ",
      "text": "\nmore than 3 but less than 6\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zUzzu",
      "text": "\nmore than 6 but less than 9\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qZjo7",
      "text": "\nmore than 9\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wThmC",
      "text": "\nless than 3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{r} \\times \\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{l} \\times \\alpha$\n$2\\left(20 \\mathrm{t}-5 \\mathrm{t}^2\\right)=10 \\alpha \\Rightarrow \\alpha=4 \\mathrm{t}-\\mathrm{t}^2$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{d} \\omega}{\\mathrm{dt}}=4 \\mathrm{t}-\\mathrm{t}^2$\n$\\mathrm{~d} \\omega=\\left(4 \\mathrm{t}^2-\\mathrm{t}^2\\right) \\mathrm{dt}$\n$\\omega=2 \\mathrm{t}^2-\\frac{\\mathrm{t}^3}{3}$ (on integration)\n$\\omega=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}=6 \\mathrm{~s}$",
    "image": null
  },
